-- The WASM spike's project file (docs/proposal-native-ports.md, host 4).
--
-- Scope is the CORE alone: glance-internal first, the public library after it
-- compiles.  glance-web, the CLI and the native window stay out — the page
-- itself is the host on this target, and the transport seam replaces HTTP.
--
-- Build with the ghc-wasm-meta toolchain on PATH:
--   make wasm-spike
packages: .
          -- text-show as upstream cut it, with the line marked `glance:'
          -- moved to the RTS's 64-bit thread id: its rts_getThreadId import
          -- said CInt, and wasm-ld checks foreign signatures where native
          -- linkers let the mismatch slide.  Keeps upstream's name and
          -- version, so this local copy shadows Hackage's — the vendored gi
          -- packages' own rule.  Out of cabal.project for the same reason
          -- they are: a local package is built whether or not anything
          -- depends on it.
          vendored/text-show-3.11.4

-- The first measured wall (2026-08-05): crypton is unbuildable here in both
-- directions — current versions lean on mmap through `ram`, older ones on
-- basement's cbits — so the build takes the pure-crypto seam instead.
package glance
  flags: +pure-crypto

-- The spike's expected walls, recorded ahead of the run so the catalog reads
-- against a prediction: `unix` (Data.Org.Walk's lstat discipline) has only a
-- partial WASI story, and crypton's digests may lean on C.  Whatever fails
-- here is the measured input to the platform seam the ports proposal defers.
